# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Participant data -- NEVER commit. HRD_RAW_MinuteLevel.csv is minute-level
# heart rate / sleep / screen / call data with depression labels for 166 people
# and is covered by the study's data agreement, not by this repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
datasets/*.csv
datasets/cache/
results/
datasets/HRD_RAW_MinuteLevel.csv
*.csv.gz
*.parquet

# Model weights: encoder.pt is ~235 MB each, well over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt

# Run outputs. Since 2026-09-18 there is exactly ONE location for experiment output,
# results/, and every fold in it carries a manifest.json recording the git commit, the
# data cache hash and the participant split (docs/OUTPUT_PROVENANCE.md). The three names
# below are the pre-rescue generation: they had no provenance metadata and were removed,
# and the rules stay so that recreating them cannot stage anything.
results/
results_hrd/
results_hrd_energy/
results_globem/
logs/
slurm-*.out

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Transfer archives: the tarballs used to push code to the cluster and pull
# results back. Both are derived -- the working tree is the source of truth for
# what goes up, and results/ (already ignored) for what comes down.
*.tgz
*.tar.gz

# Scratch trees from local one-off tests. Named with a leading underscore so
# they sort together and never collide with a real package.
/_*/

# Stray caches. tasks/rhythm.py writes paper_cosinor_topk<N>_cache.npz next to
# the variant dir; running against a variant dir at the repo root lands it here
# instead of under results/.
/*.npz
_randinit_cache/
audit_fast_*.json
architecture_loss.json
readout_sweep.json
noise_branch_ceiling.json
dispersion_ceiling.json
kfold_eval.json
kfold_null.json

# analysis artifacts: the numbers live in results/results_summary.csv, the JSONs are scratch
*.log
# trend_causality.json is tracked under results/
kfold_null.json
trend_causality.json
block_pretext.log
sanity.log
pretext_gate.log

# Runner output: plan.json plus per-fold artifacts.
runs/
metrics.json

# Retired code kept for reference only, and the manuscript (its own repository).
archive/
SSL_Rhythmicity/
docs/audit/evidence/

# Artefacts of the cluster round-trip documented in CLUSTER.md. All are regenerable: the
# bundle from `git archive HEAD`, the extracted copy from that bundle, and the downloaded
# results from the cluster. None belongs in the repository, and each has staged participant
# data at some point -- rhythmssl_rescue/ carries its own datasets/cache/ one level down, so
# the cache rule above does not reach it.
rhythmssl_rescue/
rescue_upload.tgz
rescue_results_*/

# Written by scripts/stamp_version.py for the cluster copy; derived from git.
CODE_VERSION
